  "id": "tbilisi_sazandari",
  "name": "Sazandari (Tbilisi tar, kamancha and daira ensemble)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The Eastern-oriented strand of Tbilisi's urban music, played by sazandari trios of tar, kamancha and daira frame drum at feasts and in the taverns of the old city, sharing modes and repertoire with Persian, Armenian and Azerbaijani urban traditions; the doira card stands for the daira, and the kamancha card keeps its Garabagh-school setting, the nearest Caucasian one it offers. Songs attributed to the eighteenth-century Tbilisi bard Sayat-Nova belong to its repertoire, and the ensembles were recorded by Melodiya and the Tbilisi Conservatoire.",
  "recipe": "classic modern sazandari, ballad Poetry, med east poetic branch. many notes per syllable, solo with instrumental accompaniment. caucasian urban tar azerbaijani, walnut bowl skin faced canonical caucasian garabagh shusha mugham school canonical azerbaijani kamancha, doira frame drum. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
